Pull the capture sets out of an inferred intersection again

scala/scala3 #27539 stopped Setup from rewriting `A^{c1} & B^{c2}` to
`(A & B)^{c1 ** c2}`, because the meet of two sets whose elements are known
only later can come out too small. That is not so where a set is a variable
Setup has just made for an inferred type, and without the rewrite the type
inferred for an instance of an anonymous class with several parents keeps one
capture set per parent, `((Handle^) & (Granting[Int]^)){type Under = fs}`.
From 3.10.2-RC1 on such an instance

  - did not conform to a parameter of the same intersection type with a
    single capture set ("capability any cannot flow into capture set {any}"),
  - was not made pure by `caps.unsafe.unsafeAssumePure`, which strips the
    capture set of its argument's type.

The rewrite is made again for inferred types, where at least one of the two
sets is a variable.

Found in Soundness's galilei (directory handles) and parasite (daemon and
task handles).

